WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.581
A first-time donor gives on a Tuesday.

2
00:00:02.591 --> 00:00:06.331
Two weeks later, a welcome arrives with a
report made just for them.

3
00:00:06.341 --> 00:00:08.781
And nobody on your team had to press send.

4
00:00:08.791 --> 00:00:11.080
It takes three things you may already
have:

5
00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:15.782
your CRM, a personalized Storyraise
report, and an email platform with

6
00:00:15.792 --> 00:00:18.151
automations or journeys.

7
00:00:18.161 --> 00:00:19.806
Start with one report.

8
00:00:19.902 --> 00:00:24.165
Merge tags, like a first name, fill in
differently for every donor who opens it.

9
00:00:24.175 --> 00:00:26.656
You publish it once.

10
00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:31.547
Next, connect your CRM in the Connections
tab, and turn on Auto-sync.

11
00:00:31.557 --> 00:00:36.145
New donors in your CRM become Storyraise
constituents on their own, with no uploads

12
00:00:36.155 --> 00:00:39.367
and no one opening the dashboard.

13
00:00:40.361 --> 00:00:42.894
Now choose Send in an email on your
report.

14
00:00:42.904 --> 00:00:47.120
Paste your email platform's merge tag for
the donor's email address, and copy the

15
00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:47.985
link.

16
00:00:48.198 --> 00:00:51.926
Every email carries that one link, and
each donor's copy fills in with their own

17
00:00:51.936 --> 00:00:53.390
address.

18
00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:57.065
In your email platform, build the journey
the way you already do.

19
00:00:57.278 --> 00:01:00.902
A first gift starts it, it waits two
weeks, then it sends a welcome email with

20
00:01:00.912 --> 00:01:02.527
a button that uses your link.

21
00:01:02.537 --> 00:01:05.990
Your platform decides who gets it, and
when.

22
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.821
When a donor clicks, Storyraise looks them
up right then, and the report greets them

23
00:01:09.831 --> 00:01:10.919
by name.

24
00:01:11.016 --> 00:01:14.384
That includes donors who joined long after
you published, so there's nothing to

25
00:01:14.394 --> 00:01:16.631
republish.

26
00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:20.748
And because every link is personal,
Analytics shows you who read their

27
00:01:20.758 --> 00:01:25.584
welcome, by name, so you know who to thank
next.

28
00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.669
The same setup works for other moments,
too:

29
00:01:28.882 --> 00:01:32.935
a giving anniversary, a year-end impact
report, or a check-in with a donor you

30
00:01:32.945 --> 00:01:34.910
haven't heard from.

31
00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:37.981
The step-by-step setup is right here on
this page.
